# Baseline for dev/check_upstream_test_copies.py — the upstream-test-copy differential.
#
# Format: `<node id pattern>  # reason`, one per line. Every entry MUST carry a reason;
# the script refuses to run otherwise (so does a duplicate pattern, or a pattern that
# does not start with one of the three owned test files). The pattern is a repo-relative
# node id of the ORIGINAL file, e.g.
#
#     mlx_vlm/tests/test_server.py::TestCompaction::test_max_output_is_a_ceiling[*-chat-*]
#
# `*` is the only wildcard (any run of characters, including none); brackets are
# literal; the whole id must match. A pattern with no `[` also matches every
# parametrization of that test. Prefer the exact parameters that fail: a bare
# test name also excuses a future regression in the parameters that pass today.
# A whole copy that fails to import is the id `mlx_vlm/tests/<file>.py` (no `::`).
#
# What this audit catches: the fork OWNS test_speculative.py, test_server.py and
# test_generate.py (C104), so upstream's own assertions in them never run against the
# fork's library. The audit runs upstream's copies (at --upstream-ref) against this
# tree and fails on any failing test this file does not excuse. It found a real bug
# the first time it was run by hand: a standalone `glm_moe_dsa_mtp` drafter loaded
# with every weight silently dropped. `dev/ci.py` passes it `.upstream-sync-ref`.
#
# THE TRAP, the same one as .call-argument-exclusions and .body-divergence-exclusions:
# do not excuse a failure by asserting that the fork changed the behaviour on purpose.
# Establish provenance first — `git log -S'<the asserted literal>'` and the test's own
# commit — and say what you established: either upstream's test is stale/wrong, or the
# fork deliberately diverges (name where it is recorded). An excused failure is
# invisible to every later run; "fails on upstream's tree too" is a valid reason only
# if you ran it there.
#
# A stale entry (matches no failing test) is reported under `warning:` and does not
# gate; prune it in the same commit that fixed the cause.
#
# Validate that the audit FIRES (an audit never seen to fail cannot be trusted green):
#   1. delete one entry below (or, with the baseline complete, revert a fork fix that an
#      upstream assertion covers);
#   2. run `python dev/check_upstream_test_copies.py --upstream-ref <sync-ref>`;
#   3. expect exit 1 naming exactly the uncovered ids; restore the entry;
#   4. `git status --porcelain --ignored mlx_vlm/tests` must show no `test_zz_up_` path.
# `--list` prints every failing id, ready to paste here without its reason.
#
# Validated 2026-10-26 against e9af3766: reverting the founding fix (mlx_vlm/utils.py stripping
# `mtp.*` unconditionally) made it exit 1 naming 3 NEW
# test_load_registered_native_drafter[...glm_moe_dsa...] ids; restored, exit 0. That instance is
# also covered by the fork's own tests/test_load_model_mtp_weights.py since the sync.
#
# Seeded 2026-10-26 from a run against e9af3766: 49 failing ids in 16 test functions, every
# one fork divergence or a recorded upstream bug. No new gap.

